definitionOfDone:
Identities derive only from transferred bytes:
- an entry with a declared identity or any other extra key is refused with SNAPSHOT_ENTRY_INVALID;
- size and sha256 come from a private copy that the manifest returns, so mutating the caller's buffer afterwards changes neither;
- the digest does not depend on input order, and it changes when any byte, path, executable bit or entry kind changes.

implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of the diff, scoped to this security gate. Load adversarial-self-review.

Try to get bytes past it:
- a spoofed own byteLength, a resizable or detached ArrayBuffer, a Buffer subclass;
- getters that mutate an earlier entry after it was measured;
- symbol keys, a null-prototype entry, an Array subclass, a sparse array;
- '.GIT', '.git.', 'GIT~1', ZWNJ, decomposed accents, 'ß'/'SS', ancestor or descendant pairs;
- '.git/CON' (must be CONTROL_PATH);
- an over-long path under .git (PATH_INVALID is accepted: bound first).

Also check:
- No hashing happens before every bound and collision check has passed.
- No message can echo input.
- The framing is unambiguous (length-prefixed) and versioned.
- The sort is by UTF-8 bytes, not UTF-16.
- Only node:crypto is imported.
- Nothing outside the three files changed: git diff --stat, peers excluded.

Fix any finding, then rerun step 4 before moe.complete_task.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
Conventions come from scripts/local-runner/guest-bridge.mjs:
- a header comment citing facts;
- a fixed-text MESSAGES map, and bridgeError(code) falling back to an INPUT_INVALID code;
- isRecord (Object.prototype or null prototype) and exactKeys helpers;
- Object.freeze on every result;
- a Buffer global with no import.
Its tests (local-runner-bridge.test.mjs) use refuses(fn, code, label) and table rows.

The CI step 'Test local runner prerequisite bundles' runs in build-all-platforms on ubuntu, windows and macos, so the tests must be platform-pure.

Limits from mem:gotcha-local-runner-tests and mem:gotcha-local-runner-cross-platform-tests:
- the global forbidden pattern (the double-underscore proto key) applies to test strings;
- QA counts additions + deletions against 400, comments and blank lines included;
- the Linux gate env is env -i with nvm node v24.21.0;
- Windows node runs from the /mnt/d repo root.
